Calibration of non-automatic weighing instruments — EURAMET cg-18 (@met-weighing: 0, is #reference, #part-of @met-sources) { r_5VF8R8DG8XMTSHWXG8Y32AJYCQ
EURAMET Technical Committee for Mass and Related Quantities. Guidelines on the Calibration of Non-Automatic Weighing Instruments, calibration guide 18, version 4.0, November 2015. English.

[Official calibration-guide catalogue and PDF download, No. 18](https://www.euramet.org/publications-media-centre/calibration-guidelines).

Read the complete guide for weighing behavior, comparison sequences, corrections, uncertainty, and reporting. Reconstruct an uncertainty example and distinguish the instrument’s calibration from the uncertainty of a subsequent weighing under changed load, environment, and handling. Consult the actual manufacturer’s conditions before translating a paper study into laboratory work.

The official catalogue identified this edition on 28 October 2026. The automated download endpoint timed out during checking; the catalogue’s identity and download reference were accessible. EURAMET retains copyright and guide-specific reproduction/translation terms; free access is not assumed to permit arbitrary extracts or adaptation. No copy is bundled.

**Return:** [Measurement and metrology sources — books, guides, and research](../Sources.lingua#r_6H584EJ2Z9D11PG89Y21Y8T1A3).
